WEBVTT

00:00:33.564 --> 00:00:36.150
(girls laughing)

00:00:36.233 --> 00:00:38.152
Shame you're not as quick as me, Ed!

00:00:38.235 --> 00:00:40.529
(Susan) Last one in's a rotten egg.

00:00:40.613 --> 00:00:45.201
- Watch out!
- Here it comes!

00:00:53.417 --> 00:00:55.085
Wait a minute!

00:00:58.881 --> 00:01:00.508
(Edmund) Come on,
Susan. Hurry up!

00:01:00.591 --> 00:01:03.177
Come on, it's lovely.

00:01:05.429 --> 00:01:08.974
- (Susan) Edmund.
- (laughing)

00:01:09.058 --> 00:01:12.102
(Susan) Ed? Ed!

00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:19.527
- What is it?
- Where do you suppose we are?

00:01:19.610 --> 00:01:21.487
Where do you think?

00:01:21.570 --> 00:01:24.448
Well, I don't remember
any ruins in Narnia.

00:01:46.303 --> 00:01:50.266
(birds chirping, insects buzzing)

00:02:17.710 --> 00:02:19.461
Wonder who lived here.

00:02:27.177 --> 00:02:29.179
I think we did.

00:02:37.563 --> 00:02:39.106
Hey, that's mine.

00:02:39.189 --> 00:02:41.609
- From my chess set.
- Which chess set?

00:02:41.692 --> 00:02:45.112
I didn't exactly have a solid gold
chess set in Finchley, did I?

00:02:50.701 --> 00:02:52.161
Can't be.

00:02:59.668 --> 00:03:01.503
- Don't you see?
- What?

00:03:03.380 --> 00:03:04.715
Imagine walls.

00:03:07.718 --> 00:03:09.386
And columns, there.

00:03:13.891 --> 00:03:16.310
(Lucy) And a glass roof.

00:03:24.735 --> 00:03:26.278
Cair Paravel.

00:03:28.781 --> 00:03:32.409
(horses galloping)

00:03:34.828 --> 00:03:37.081
(baby cooing)

00:04:01.605 --> 00:04:05.192
Wait. Wait, my lord.
It is not what you think.

00:04:05.275 --> 00:04:07.528
Then what is it?

00:04:07.611 --> 00:04:09.446
We're not exactly sure.

00:04:14.785 --> 00:04:16.704
Impossible.

00:04:26.213 --> 00:04:30.634
I warned this council when it
put its trust in Lord Miraz...

00:04:31.760 --> 00:04:34.221
- ...there would be consequences.
- No.

00:04:34.304 --> 00:04:37.182
We can't accuse the
Lord Protector without proof.

00:04:37.266 --> 00:04:40.352
How long are we going
to hide behind that excuse?

00:04:40.436 --> 00:04:43.647
Until every chair
in this chamber is empty?

00:04:45.482 --> 00:04:48.902
Lords of the council,
my apologies for being late.

00:04:48.986 --> 00:04:51.697
I wasn't aware we were in session.

00:04:51.780 --> 00:04:54.867
No doubt you were otherwise occupied.

00:04:57.119 --> 00:04:59.079
My lord?

00:04:59.163 --> 00:05:02.958
Ever since the death
of Caspian the ninth,

00:05:03.042 --> 00:05:06.420
you've behaved as if you were king.

00:05:06.503 --> 00:05:10.716
Now it seems that from behind his walls
even Prince Caspian has gone missing.

00:05:11.717 --> 00:05:15.137
My deepest condolences,
Lord Miraz.

00:05:15.220 --> 00:05:18.432
Imagine, losing your nephew,

00:05:18.515 --> 00:05:20.934
the rightful heir to the throne,

00:05:21.018 --> 00:05:24.563
on the very night your wife
has blessed you with a son.

00:05:25.898 --> 00:05:28.317
Thank you, Lord Sopespian.

00:05:28.400 --> 00:05:31.737
Your compassion is a boon
in this troubled time.

00:05:31.820 --> 00:05:35.449
I trust you can tell us how such
a tragedy could have occurred.

00:05:35.532 --> 00:05:37.117
(door opens)

00:05:41.371 --> 00:05:44.500
That is the most disturbing news of all.

00:05:49.213 --> 00:05:53.926
Our beloved Caspian was abducted...

00:05:54.009 --> 00:05:55.719
(men murmuring)

00:05:57.387 --> 00:05:59.348
...by Narnians.

00:05:59.431 --> 00:06:02.434
- (men shouting)
- You go too far, Miraz.

00:06:02.518 --> 00:06:07.189
Expect us to stand by while you blame
such a blatant crime on fairy tales?

00:06:13.237 --> 00:06:15.906
- What?
- (men talking, indistinct)

00:06:17.658 --> 00:06:23.247
We forget, my lords...
Narnia was once a savage land.

00:06:23.330 --> 00:06:26.667
Fierce creatures roamed free.

00:06:26.750 --> 00:06:30.420
Much of our forefathers' blood was shed

00:06:30.504 --> 00:06:34.258
to exterminate this vermin.

00:06:39.012 --> 00:06:41.390
Or so we thought.

00:06:41.473 --> 00:06:45.477
But while we've been bickering
amongst ourselves...

00:06:47.062 --> 00:06:51.817
...they've been breeding
like cockroaches under a rock!

00:06:51.900 --> 00:06:55.612
Growing stronger. Watching us.

00:06:58.532 --> 00:07:00.617
Waiting to strike!

00:07:05.205 --> 00:07:09.126
And you wonder why we don't like you.

00:07:10.586 --> 00:07:14.214
Well, I intend to strike back.

00:07:16.258 --> 00:07:20.053
Even if I have to cut down
the entire forest...

00:07:20.137 --> 00:07:24.141
...I assure you,
I will find Prince Caspian

00:07:24.224 --> 00:07:28.395
and finish what our ancestors began.

00:07:46.163 --> 00:07:48.498
- Catapults.
- What?

00:07:49.833 --> 00:07:54.004
This didn't just happen.
Cair Paravel was attacked.

